<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Twin Lakes Trail and Loop (from Barlow Pass Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:172-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.282436" lon="-121.685554"><ele>1267.4</ele><name>Barlow Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:barlow-pass-sno-park (OSM way 129814976); confidence: high; pdf_page: 174; book_elev_ft: 4157; quote: From the northeast corner of Barlow Pass Sno-Park climb the snow bank, go several yards, turn right (south), and ski through big timber along the Pacific Crest Trail (PCT).</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.257842" lon="-121.691693"><ele>1327.6</ele><name>PCT / Upper Twin Lake Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 3771397418, north end of Twin Lakes Trail #495 on the PCT; confidence: high; pdf_page: 175; quote: descends gently along the east side of Ghost Ridge, and 2.3 miles from the trailhead is the junction of the PCT with the side trail to the Upper Twin Lake Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.244899" lon="-121.676587"><ele>1341.0</ele><name>Upper Twin Lake, south end</name><desc>source: OSM node 495566423 on Twin Lakes Trail #495 at the south end of Upper Twin Lake (OSM way 40773969); confidence: high; pdf_page: 175; book_elev_ft: 4400; quote: up two switchbacks to Bird Butte Pass at 4,500 feet ... descends moderately ... to the upper lake at 4,400 feet. The trail goes along the east shore to the south end</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.239891" lon="-121.677555"><ele>1293.0</ele><name>Near Lower Twin Lake (north shore)</name><desc>source: OSM node 495566526 on Twin Lakes Trail #495 where a side path (way 73150930) leaves toward Lower Twin Lake (OSM way 40773962); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 175; book_elev_ft: 4160; quote: follow the moderately steep trail down to the lower lake ... From the lower lake ... ski up the draw 150 yards, turn left (west), and follow the loop trail over a low pass, then down to the PCT</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.237041" lon="-121.686448"><ele>1340.3</ele><name>PCT / Lower Twin Lake Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 985022356, south end of Twin Lakes Trail #495 on the PCT; confidence: high; pdf_page: 175; quote: At 1.5 miles a side trail to Lower Twin Lake leaves the PCT at a right angle, climbing gently eastward for 100 yards to a pass at 4,460 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.282436" lon="-121.685554"><ele>1267.4</ele><name>Barlow Pass Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 175; quote: Then follow the PCT north to Barlow Pass Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Twin Lakes Trail and Loop (from Barlow Pass Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Barlow Pass Sno-Park -&gt; PCT / Upper Twin Lake Trail junction: osm (high), 1.90 mi | 2. PCT / Upper Twin Lake Trail junction -&gt; Upper Twin Lake, south end: osm (high), 1.63 mi | 3. Upper Twin Lake, south end -&gt; Near Lower Twin Lake (north shore): osm (high), 0.72 mi | 4. Near Lower Twin Lake (north shore) -&gt; PCT / Lower Twin Lake Trail junction: osm (high), 0.67 mi | 5. PCT / Lower Twin Lake Trail junction -&gt; Barlow Pass Sno-Park (finish): osm (high), 3.46 mi</desc>
